      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, feeling a profound sense of disconnection and losing your core identity is a painful but documented experience that many face during major life transitions or depression. While this hollow feeling is valid and heavy, it often signals deep depression or burnout rather than actual self-destruction, suggesting that part of \"you\" is still waiting to be heard even if hidden beneath the shell. You are not your entire history, but if this darkness feels permanent, please consider speaking with a professional who can help you navigate this loss without judging you for wanting to rest.",
